## 1) Core UX requirements (must implement)
### 1.1 Plan library
- Allow user to upload and manage multiple plan PDFs (plans have versions/revisions).
- Show a “Plans” page/list with:
  - plan name, revision, upload date, file size
  - open plan button
- Persist plans in storage/ and metadata in DB (or a metadata JSON file if DB isn’t set up yet; DB preferred).

### 1.2 PDF plan viewer
- Render PDF pages with PDF.js (likely already present or can be added under vendor/).
- Must support:
  - pinch-zoom, pan, page navigation
  - fast rendering on Android tablet
- Overlay layer:
  - a transparent HTML overlay above the canvas where pins are drawn
  - pins remain correctly positioned while zooming/panning

### 1.3 Pins / Annotations (snags / survey points)
- On tap, place a pin at the tapped location. Immediately open an “Issue” side panel / modal:
  - Title (short)
  - Notes (long)
  - Category (dropdown: Safety, Quality, Design, Access, MEP, Fire, Snag, Other)
  - Status (dropdown: Open, In Progress, Closed)
  - Priority (Low/Medium/High)
  - Trade (optional text)
  - Assigned to (optional)
  - Due date (optional)
- Each pin stores:
  - plan_id
  - page number
  - x, y in PDF page coordinates OR normalized coordinates (0..1) that are resolution-independent
  - created_at, updated_at, created_by (optional)
- Pins are displayed as:
  - numbered markers (S01, S02, …) or sequential numeric per plan/revision
  - color/shape depends on status (Open/In Progress/Closed)
- Provide:
  - list view of issues for current plan (filter by status/category/priority)
  - clicking an issue jumps to page and centers the pin

### 1.4 Photo attachments
- From within an issue:
  - “Add photo” uses Android camera capture if available
  - Show thumbnails
  - Allow remove photo
- IMPORTANT: compress images client-side before upload (Android photos are huge):
  - target width 1600–2000px, JPEG quality ~0.75–0.85
  - preserve EXIF orientation if possible
- Upload photos to storage/ (subfolder per plan_id and issue_id).
- Store photo metadata in DB.

### 1.5 Autosave + reliability
- All edits autosave (debounced).
- If offline:
  - store changes locally
  - show offline indicator
  - queue uploads and issue updates to sync later

