## 2) Offline-first PWA requirements (must implement)
Yes, this MUST be a PWA:
- Add manifest.json (name, icons, start_url, display=standalone)
- Add service worker:
  - cache app shell (HTML/CSS/JS/icons)
  - cache PDF.js assets
  - cache plan PDFs when opened (so they’re available offline later)
- Offline data storage:
  - Use IndexedDB to store:
    - plan metadata (at least plan list)
    - issues JSON per plan
    - a sync queue of pending operations (create/update/delete issue, photo upload)
- Sync strategy:
  - When online, process queue FIFO:
    - POST issue changes to API
    - Upload photos (multipart/form-data)
    - Mark queue items complete on success
- UX:
  - show “Offline mode” banner
  - show “Syncing…” status and “last synced” timestamp
  - provide a manual “Sync now” button

Implementation tip:
- If no build tooling, implement a simple vanilla service worker.
- If you add Workbox, keep it minimal and committed.

